{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1378 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "81aea7ae10de29c5b7218920ac795179062b67a82e300996335655f486951d18" :edb/db-before-t 1377 :edb/db-after-t 1378 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534690 50 #inst "2026-10-08T04:17:54.940Z" 13194139534690 true] [17592186064081 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303565 13194139534690 true] [17592186064081 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303586 13194139534690 true] [17592186064081 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303607 13194139534690 true] [17592186064082 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303572 13194139534690 true] [17592186064082 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303579 13194139534690 true] [17592186064082 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303593 13194139534690 true] [17592186064082 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303600 13194139534690 true] [17592186064498 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534690 true] [17592186064498 1100 "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nFor the function $f(x) = 2x^{3} - 6x + 12$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $x =-1$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n2. $f^{″}(-1) < 0$\n3. $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x =-1$" 13194139534690 false] [17592186064498 1100 "For the function $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-6x+12,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=-1$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n- ${f}^{″}(-1)<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=-1$" 13194139534690 true] [17592186064498 1145 "We need to identify whether $x=-1$ is a critical point. If it is, we then need to classify it using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-6x+12,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=2\\cdot 3{x}^{2}-6=6{x}^{2}-6,\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-6 & =0 \\\\ 6({x}^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ 6(x+1)(x-1) & =0 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=\\pm 1.$ We're interested in the critical point $x=-1.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at this critical point. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=12x,\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=-1$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(-1)=-12<0.\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is negative at $x=-1,$ so this critical point is a relative *maximum*. \n\nTherefore, comparing our results with the given statements, we conclude that:\n\n- $x=-1$ is a critical point of $f(x)\\,✓$\n\n- ${f}^{″}(-1)<0\\,✓$\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative *maximum* at $x=-1\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139534690 true] [17592186064502 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534690 true] [17592186064502 1100 "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nConsider the function $f(x) = x^{5} + 5x^{3} - 90x + 108$. Given that $f^{′}(-\\sqrt{3}) = 0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $f^{″}(-\\sqrt{3}) < 0$\n2. $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x =-\\sqrt{3}$\n3. $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x =-\\sqrt{3}$" 13194139534690 false] [17592186064502 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{5}+5{x}^{3}-90x+108.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(-\\sqrt{3})=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(-\\sqrt{3})<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=-\\sqrt{3}$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=-\\sqrt{3}$" 13194139534690 true] [17592186064502 1145 "We're given that $x=-\\sqrt{3}$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)={x}^{5}+5{x}^{3}-90x+108,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=5{x}^{4}+15{x}^{2}-90.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=20{x}^{3}+30x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-\\sqrt{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-\\sqrt{3}) & =20{(-\\sqrt{3})}^{3}+30(-\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =20\\cdot 3(-\\sqrt{3})+30(-\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =-90\\sqrt{3}<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is negative, we conclude that $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=-\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303565 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303566 13194139534690 true] [17592186303565 1089 "q-21500" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303565 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534690 true] [17592186303565 1100 "For the function $f(x)=-3{x}^{5/2}+5{x}^{3/2}+15$ on $(0,\\infty ),$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=1$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n- ${f}^{″}(1)<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=1$" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303565 1113 #uuid "e7424056-31be-5c03-b30d-76d3e1194cad" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303565 1145 "We need to identify whether $x=1$ is a critical point. If it is, we then need to classify it using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=-3{x}^{5/2}+5{x}^{3/2}+15,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-3\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}{x}^{3/2}+5\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}{x}^{1/2}=-\\frac{15}{2}{x}^{3/2}+\\frac{15}{2}{x}^{1/2},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{15}{2}{x}^{3/2}+\\frac{15}{2}{x}^{1/2} & =0 \\\\ -\\frac{15}{2}{x}^{1/2}(x-1) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have a critical point at $x=1.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at this critical point. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=-\\frac{15}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}{x}^{1/2}+\\frac{15}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2}=-\\frac{45}{4}{x}^{1/2}+\\frac{15}{4}{x}^{-1/2},\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=1$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(1)=-\\frac{45}{4}(1)^{1/2}+\\frac{15}{4}(1)^{-1/2}=-\\frac{15}{2}<0.\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is negative at $x=1,$ so this critical point is a relative *maximum*. \n\nTherefore, comparing our results with the given statements, we conclude that:\n\n- $x=1$ is a critical point of $f(x)\\,✓$\n\n- ${f}^{″}(1)<0\\,✓$\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative *maximum* at $x=1\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303567 13194139534690 true] [17592186303566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303568 13194139534690 true] [17592186303566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303569 13194139534690 true] [17592186303566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303570 13194139534690 true] [17592186303566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303571 13194139534690 true] [17592186303566 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534690 true] [17592186303566 1041 "selection" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303566 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303570 13194139534690 true] [17592186303566 1110 #uuid "9f403874-b77e-5453-b0dd-fc42a08f3eb7" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303567 1034 "None of the statements are true" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303567 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303567 1111 #uuid "74b0353e-bafe-5d57-8d37-72e1c92e74db" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303568 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303568 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303568 1111 #uuid "591ddb1c-6d16-5956-8f0e-ff28e8c470f1" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303569 1034 "I only" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303569 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303569 1111 #uuid "e4731eb3-c838-5d5f-a4b2-516b9d92f14e" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303570 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303570 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303570 1111 #uuid "ffb347c2-9856-5f04-8482-c7ada82795cb" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303571 1034 "II only" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303571 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303571 1111 #uuid "b3c3dfe8-712a-5dde-a801-493afa1e462a" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303572 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303573 13194139534690 true] [17592186303572 1089 "q-21508" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303572 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534690 true] [17592186303572 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)=3{x}^{2}-6x+9.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(1)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(1)<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=1$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=1$" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303572 1113 #uuid "d08953a7-b9c1-53e4-92d6-e017849bbea4" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303572 1145 "We're given that $x=1$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=3{x}^{2}-6x+9,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=6x-6.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=6.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1) & =6>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is positive, we conclude that $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303574 13194139534690 true] [17592186303573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303575 13194139534690 true] [17592186303573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303576 13194139534690 true] [17592186303573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303577 13194139534690 true] [17592186303573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303578 13194139534690 true] [17592186303573 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534690 true] [17592186303573 1041 "selection" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303573 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303578 13194139534690 true] [17592186303573 1110 #uuid "f0216f1f-c5ba-5956-b2b3-3db49c2e1d2a" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303574 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303574 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303574 1111 #uuid "c17c5262-a191-5f8f-809b-35a8463a2485" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303575 1034 "I only" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303575 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303575 1111 #uuid "f8085f68-bcb5-5048-a333-8119c7f54e45" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303576 1034 "III only" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303576 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303576 1111 #uuid "772ca79f-acab-57f8-aac1-9b7ce244ec4e" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303577 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303577 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303577 1111 #uuid "121e1b32-aa44-58a6-aeaa-2df101a75838" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303578 1034 "II only" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303578 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303578 1111 #uuid "83525aaf-af2f-5586-b3d4-c0529c291449" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303579 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303580 13194139534690 true] [17592186303579 1089 "q-21541" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303579 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534690 true] [17592186303579 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)=-2{x}^{5/3}+{x}^{2/3}.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(\\frac{1}{5})=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(\\frac{1}{5})<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=\\frac{1}{5}$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=\\frac{1}{5}$" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303579 1113 #uuid "5be071e3-c224-574a-92ed-72af7b4c80c2" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303579 1145 "We're given that $x=\\frac{1}{5}$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=-2{x}^{5/3}+{x}^{2/3},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{10}{3}{x}^{2/3}+\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{-1/3}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=-\\frac{20}{9}{x}^{-1/3}-\\frac{2}{9}{x}^{-4/3}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{1}{5},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(\\frac{1}{5}) & =-\\frac{20}{9}\\cdot {5}^{1/3}-\\frac{2}{9}\\cdot {5}^{4/3}=-\\frac{10}{3}\\cdot {5}^{1/3}<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is negative, we conclude that $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=\\frac{1}{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303581 13194139534690 true] [17592186303580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303582 13194139534690 true] [17592186303580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303583 13194139534690 true] [17592186303580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303584 13194139534690 true] [17592186303580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303585 13194139534690 true] [17592186303580 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534690 true] [17592186303580 1041 "selection" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303580 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303581 13194139534690 true] [17592186303580 1110 #uuid "bb40351c-19e2-541d-80e2-bf69fe3ad102" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303581 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303581 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303581 1111 #uuid "e0d7f6c4-492c-5647-8c1b-3591f0f27fd6" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303582 1034 "I only" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303582 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303582 1111 #uuid "b3ce5e96-8993-5aa8-bc53-0d0630c04716" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303583 1034 "III only" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303583 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303583 1111 #uuid "e161399f-c327-5510-a9a3-de111d14051b" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303584 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303584 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303584 1111 #uuid "ad08725b-3681-51b8-aecb-52af410596c8" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303585 1034 "II only" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303585 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303585 1111 #uuid "a8147da4-a1f4-519d-962b-dc643ef43c80" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303586 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303587 13194139534690 true] [17592186303586 1089 "q-21812" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303586 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534690 true] [17592186303586 1100 "For the function $f(x)=-4{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+3,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(0)>0$\n- $x=0$ is a relative minimum of $f(x)$\n- ${f}^{″}(1)<0$\n- $x=1$ is a relative minimum of $f(x)$" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303586 1113 #uuid "93ba87ee-88a3-5ffc-9106-ee2a9e22d43b" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303586 1145 "We need to identify the critical points. Then, we then need to classify them using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=-4{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+3,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=12x-12{x}^{2},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12x-12{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 12x(1-x) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=0,1.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at the critical points. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=12-24x,\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at each critical point, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0) & =12>0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(1) & =-12<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that:\n\n- Statements I and II are true. The second derivative is positive at $x=0,$ so this is a relative minimum of $f(x).$\n\n- Statement III is true while statement IV is false. The second derivative is negative at $x=1,$ so this is a relative maximum of $f(x).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only\"." 13194139534690 true] [17592186303587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303588 13194139534690 true] [17592186303587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303589 13194139534690 true] [17592186303587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303590 13194139534690 true] [17592186303587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303591 13194139534690 true] [17592186303587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303592 13194139534690 true] [17592186303587 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534690 true] [17592186303587 1041 "selection" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303587 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303592 13194139534690 true] [17592186303587 1110 #uuid "e3e15259-6670-524c-b39f-555d9daf423f" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303588 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303588 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303588 1111 #uuid "e99781bc-0051-5212-a587-94137cb02638" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303589 1034 "II and IV only" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303589 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303589 1111 #uuid "e0ae39d9-85f8-5646-82c7-283ed1537163" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303590 1034 "I, III, and IV only" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303590 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303590 1111 #uuid "3b5c4c6d-ebf3-5c84-931e-1c51c659550a" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303591 1034 "III only" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303591 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303591 1111 #uuid "89ff8dbb-2320-585d-bd01-9dbda9b37b4b" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303592 1034 "I, II, and III only" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303592 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303592 1111 #uuid "f73e413d-44b1-55ff-9d1f-e977631eb493" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303593 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303594 13194139534690 true] [17592186303593 1089 "q-22164" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303593 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534690 true] [17592186303593 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+4x+16.$  Given that ${f}^{′}(-1)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(-1)=0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=-1$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=-1$" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303593 1113 #uuid "92b9bf0a-4f53-5ec3-9401-f90bf530cbdd" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303593 1145 "Calculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)={x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+4x+16$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=4{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}+12x+4=4(x+1)^{3}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=12(x+1)^{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-1$ in the second derivative,   we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1) & =12(1-1)^{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is zero, we conclude that the test is inconclusive, we need to use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's  find the stationary points. These points are the solution of the equation ${f}^{′}(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x+1)^{3} & =0 \\\\ x & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the only stationary point is $x=-1.$\n\nLet's choose auxiliary points from each side of the stationary point and evaluate the first derivative at them. We take the auxiliary points $x=-2,0$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-2) & =4(-2+1)^{3}=-4<0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(0) & =4(0+1)^{3}=4>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince the first derivative changes the sign at  $x=-1$ from minus to plus, we conclude that $x=-1$  is a local minimum\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303595 13194139534690 true] [17592186303594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303596 13194139534690 true] [17592186303594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303597 13194139534690 true] [17592186303594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303598 13194139534690 true] [17592186303594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303599 13194139534690 true] [17592186303594 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534690 true] [17592186303594 1041 "selection" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303594 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303598 13194139534690 true] [17592186303594 1110 #uuid "73c5b1af-5758-545b-8b28-55dcc88ee8d2" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303595 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303595 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303595 1111 #uuid "59feeed0-e9be-5a46-b80b-e2e9fa2d6375" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303596 1034 "I only" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303596 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303596 1111 #uuid "36f1c57b-21fc-512d-b4e8-c55c63b98cc5" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303597 1034 "III only" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303597 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303597 1111 #uuid "89e67402-095f-59dc-a7a3-f000d785249b" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303598 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303598 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534690 true] [17592186303598 1111 #uuid "971ccc0d-1941-5879-a140-4c19d9e0a657" 13194139534690 true] [17592186303599 1034 "II only" 13194139534690 true] [175921863035